[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m Let's represent \(z\) as \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\), where \(\theta\) is a real number. Then we can substitute \(z\) into the expression and find the real part.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m The expression becomes:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m (75 + 117i) \cdot 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) + \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m First, let's simplify the terms:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m (75 + 117i) \cdot 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta))
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} \cdot \frac{\cos\theta - i\sin\theta}{\cos\theta - i\sin\theta} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4(\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta)} = \frac{96\cos\theta + 144\sin\theta + i(144\cos\theta - 96\sin\theta)}{4} = 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=169544)[0m 
